; THE WESTERN WILDS (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild) — the bandit camp beyond Tarn's Landing.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT THIS REPLACED. Two tents, a campfire and three pickups at the exact centre of a flat
; 50 x 40 field, with two rock cubes and two pines scattered around them and a straight 4.5 m track
; running in from the east seam. Nothing was hidden, nothing was defensible, and there was no reason
; to approach from one side rather than another.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW — a corrie with one throat:
;   x 2..25, z -8..6    THE APRON. Open scrub the track crosses, with scree and dead pines. You can
;                       see the rock wall from here and you cannot see what is behind it.
;   (-5, 0)             THE THROAT. Two rock masses at z = ±5 leave a five-metre gap and it is the
;                       only way in on the flat. Watch Rock stands just inside it at (-2, -10).
;   x -22..-7, z -12..10  THE CAMP BOWL. Three tents on the rim, the fire near the middle, the loot
;                       scattered between them. Everything the cell holds is in here and none of it
;                       is visible from the apron.
;   about (-6, -12)     THE SCRAMBLE. One deliberate gap in the northern lip, between RimNE and Watch
;                       Rock, about 2.6 m wide. It is the reward for walking the rock line instead of
;                       the track, and it enters the bowl behind the tents.
;
; ⚠️ NODE SCALE SCALES THE COLLIDER HERE. Every Rim*/Throat*/Scree* node is an instance of
; prp_rock_cluster whose CollisionShape3D is a child, so the node's basis scale multiplies the 3.5 m
; Shape_rock as well as the mesh. A rim rock at scale 2.0 is a SEVEN-metre collider, which is how the
; first pass of this rebuild sealed the throat completely while looking correct in the file. The rim
; runs 1.6-1.8 and the throat pair 1.5, which leaves 4.8 m of walkable gap between their colliders.
; (RockN, RockS, Tent1 and Tent2 use the older convention — node scale 1, an oversized Model child —
; so their colliders are the authored 3.5 m and 2.5 m. Do not copy one pattern onto the other.)

